{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122778","id":4351538233,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABA180OQ","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122778","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122778.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122778.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122778","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122778/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122778/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122778/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/ba77471a3f98a0090f102e1c70fe6cf764384c99","number":122778,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Add editor setting for 3D Freelook global Y vertical movement","user":{"login":"Dollengo","id":131563888,"node_id":"U_kgDOB9eBcA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131563888?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dollengo","html_url":"https://github.com/Dollengo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dollengo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dollengo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dollengo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dollengo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dollengo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dollengo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dollengo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dollengo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dollengo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"### Problem\r\nWhen navigating the 3D editor viewport in Free Look / Fly mode with the default navigation scheme (`FREELOOK_DEFAULT`), pressing `E` (up) or `Q` (down) while looking downward caused the camera to drift diagonally forward/backward due to the `up` vector being calculated from the camera's local pitch orientation.\r\n\r\n### Solution\r\n- Added a new Editor Setting `editors/3d/freelook/freelook_vertical_movement_global` (enabled by default).\r\n- When enabled (`true`), Free Look vertical motion keys (`E` and `Q`) move strictly along the global world Y axis (`Vector3(0, 1, 0)`), preventing unintended horizontal drift regardless of camera pitch angle.\r\n- When disabled (`false`), behavior falls back to camera-relative pitch orientation in the Default navigation scheme.\r\n- Forward/backward and strafe keys (`W`, `A`, `S`, `D`) remain camera-oriented.\r\n- Added automated unit tests in `tests/scene/test_view_3d_controller.cpp` verifying pitch independence, zero horizontal drift, and toggling of the setting.\r\n\r\n### How to test\r\n1. Open the 3D editor viewport.\r\n2. In Free Look mode (holding Right Mouse Button), tilt the camera downwards and press `E` or `Q`.\r\n3. Verify that vertical elevation occurs purely along the world vertical axis with zero forward/backward drift.\r\n4. Go to **Editor Settings > Editors > 3D > Freelook**, disable `Freelook Vertical Movement Global`, and verify that movement behaves relative to camera pitch.\r\n5. Run unit tests via `./bin/godot.windows.editor.x86_64.console.exe --test --test-case=\"*[View3DController]*\"`.\r\n","labels":[{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-08-24T19:04:56Z","updated_at":"2026-08-24T19:06:42Z","closed_at":"2026-08-24T19:06:39Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"404b4d3c632308ef87245c8c9cd8b84eef27f77d","ass